#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059452 :question/id #uuid "14e05d4f-373c-5d1f-aa59-7ee52466480e" :question/math-academy-id "e-14762" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\left| {\\begin{array}{ccc}0 & - 3 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8 \\\\ - 6 & - 12 & 1\\end{array}}\n\\right|.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & =0\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 8 \\\\ -12 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-(-3)\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+6\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0(8+96)+3(8+48)+6(-96+48) \\\\  & =0+3\\cdot 56+6\\cdot (-48) \\\\  & =168-288 \\\\  & =-120\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059453 :question/id #uuid "d7516cec-bd96-59db-98cd-5d82e41fa719" :question/math-academy-id "e-14763" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $A$ given below?\n\n- $\\det(A) = 0$\n\n- $A$ is **not** a singular matrix\n\n- $A$ is a singular matrix\n\n$$\nA={\\left[ \\begin{array}{ccc}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 7\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 7\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 7\\end{vmatrix}+3\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(0-4)-2(7-3)+3(4-0) \\\\  & =-4-2\\cdot 4+3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-4-8+12 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\det(A)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059454 :question/id #uuid "7780340c-43d6-5d38-9270-865914098218" :question/math-academy-id "e-14764" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of  $\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ k & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ is $2,$ find the value of the constant $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ k & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & =3\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}k & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+2\\begin{vmatrix}k & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3(12-10)-1(3k-0)+2(2k-0) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 3k+2\\cdot 2k \\\\  & =6-3k+4k \\\\  & =k+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $2,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k+6 & =2 \\\\ k & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059566 :question/id #uuid "7bfcfcbb-6212-5f9b-90aa-c79fbf7221e9" :question/math-academy-id "e-4518" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y &=1 \\\\ x-8y-z &=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{a} & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 3 & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{b} & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{c} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n\n\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y+0z &=1 \\\\ x-8y-z &=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{6} & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 3 & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{-2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n\n\nTherefore, $a=6,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059567 :question/id #uuid "c4af8b0d-e4ee-56f4-9cf6-594530639339" :question/math-academy-id "e-4519" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z &=4 \\\\ z-x+2 &=-1 \\\\ 2y-2x-4z &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{a} & 1 \\\\ \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{b} & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{c} \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z &=4 \\\\ -x+0y+z &=-3 \\\\ -2x+2y-4z &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{0} & 1 \\\\ \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{-2} & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{-3} \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n\n\nTherefore $a=0,$ $b=-2,$ $c=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059953 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8520c3ec-4c15-50b8-a223-215b84117916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a = 0, b =-5, c = 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056078} {:answer/id #uuid "c054a405-cfc8-5d5f-9ac0-022f66c16931" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a = 3, b = 5, c =-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056079} {:answer/id #uuid "ca263a82-b264-514f-9aa3-5c88fa6e33cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a = 0, b =-5, c = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056080} {:answer/id #uuid "4ccb20d2-3443-5bc1-8956-1b0a07adcd27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a = 3, b = 5, c = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056081} {:answer/id #uuid "74ba787c-95b8-57a2-b861-ace5bfec105b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a = 0, b = 5, c =-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056082}] :answer-field/id #uuid "0c1f700f-344d-5617-a2a8-e1023b26f6de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056077}] :question/id #uuid "6a1b7a71-ea24-5f1c-be92-41b7146b85c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-10000" :question/problem "The system of equations\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2y + 3z &=-1 - x \\\\ 4y &=-5z \\\\ x + 6z - 3 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & b \\\\ 1 & a & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}c \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a, b$ and $c$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060020 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc68d302-4e05-53f4-a13b-62357c5a7653" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439477} {:answer/id #uuid "3bd87d1e-fd23-5dab-bc43-900e69f9433c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439478}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186439477} :answer-field/id #uuid "91107b81-23d7-5b15-b57e-bf4ab1565fe8" :answer-field/key "$det(M)=10$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440096} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70ca64ce-81b4-5636-ba58-791451017b65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439479} {:answer/id #uuid "e05c2887-d7f6-57d2-a4c2-2f2da18a616f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439480}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186439479} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2548bbb-9529-57ff-80c9-7eb2135baee7" :answer-field/key "$det(M)=-5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440097} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b319f9de-b31e-5b7f-b008-19047e4bc681" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439481} {:answer/id #uuid "7743ec0d-8e7c-52c8-b5bf-a2c3ff1639ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439482}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186439482} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3fd9d3c-6b34-5cd5-b3aa-e7329f24b386" :answer-field/key "$M$ is a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440098} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8899c4e3-2645-5f8b-9127-fbf8c6f48ee4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667932} {:answer/id #uuid "478db39d-a240-5926-ab48-11c8e190272d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667933}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186667932} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae205eab-db1e-56c2-ac7d-5bc619d0d0ac" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668243}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d0d9bc49-c94e-5174-9068-2abf75c42684" :question/math-academy-id "q-128490" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $M$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt{5} & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix}-0\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 4\\end{vmatrix}+\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ -3\\sqrt{5} & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}(12-15)-0+\\frac{1}{3}(0+9\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\cdot (-3)+\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 9\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =-3\\sqrt{5}+3\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(M)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement “$M$ is a singular matrix” is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060276 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "099fa1e0-d872-5eb5-81ed-b3b1edaada04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=-6,\\,c=11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321222} {:answer/id #uuid "138e861a-0cc2-58a9-9676-1ec3e92f91ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=-6,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321303} {:answer/id #uuid "7024eba8-43e2-5236-ad74-99d0c32d9f47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=-4,\\,b=-4,\\,c=11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322019} {:answer/id #uuid "806f8895-3e66-5150-bdff-c12b2f1ea7b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=11,\\,c=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322157} {:answer/id #uuid "ce2f6adf-c8fe-58ac-9550-1c74ef4b3ac8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=11,\\,b=-4,\\,c=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322755}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321222} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbe13b71-8293-5712-8025-31df3dbc7ef9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323607}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5006a5f1-0a5e-50bb-a47b-7da41b1e709f" :question/math-academy-id "q-36181" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y+z &=2 \\\\ x-6y+11z &=3 \\\\ 3x-4y-z &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 & a \\\\ 1 & b & c \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 11 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 11 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,\\,b=-6,\\,c=11.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060277 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95c60b2a-194d-505f-801d-b642b8d5f5ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a = 6, b =-8, c =-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058285} {:answer/id #uuid "0883bc07-91cf-5cb0-94a7-a183fb2b8093" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a = 5, b = 8, c = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058286} {:answer/id #uuid "16cdaee5-2022-5f46-b3a5-8ab4a158cad4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a = 5, b = 8, c =-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058287} {:answer/id #uuid "28f939ee-f0c9-599c-834a-2bd50f55c7ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a = 6, b = 0, c = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058288} {:answer/id #uuid "30ddafd0-59d6-557e-b5af-a34b20845676" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a = 5, b =-4, c = 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058289}] :answer-field/id #uuid "15271f0f-aeb5-5bda-944e-c54b67eef4d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058284}] :question/id #uuid "61d02474-f2c0-5a11-b107-93d690d3e573" :question/math-academy-id "q-36184" :question/problem "The system of equations\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x + 6y + 5z &=3 \\\\ x - 4y + 8z &=1 \\\\ - 2y + 8z &=7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 & a \\\\ 1 & -4 & b \\\\ c & -2 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a, b$ and $c$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060278 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98f5e0e0-c541-5d5e-b120-030d10523d76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058291} {:answer/id #uuid "b4a5c589-e2fa-52d4-bdc2-98052caa1a12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058292} {:answer/id #uuid "050bb88d-1c57-5dcc-9cba-c9dddc9dd491" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058293} {:answer/id #uuid "287927b3-cd33-5f0b-a23f-da8c2dcc0f8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058294} {:answer/id #uuid "5a082a8b-804e-590d-a86c-ce9acb67344c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058295}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f30ee70b-e1cf-592b-a7b7-c7aab8026e36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058290}] :question/id #uuid "30744632-a42a-5c58-b02f-ea2283f92b9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-38128" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{vmatrix}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060446 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f01712c7-1167-5ce2-b75e-faae0fd6dd90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440011} {:answer/id #uuid "b1d67a8b-60f6-5699-b39d-4d178f673f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440012}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440012} :answer-field/id #uuid "61f5a057-7cb0-51ea-b996-75db0a60dff4" :answer-field/key "$x=-8$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440363} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6fca5a5-1769-5de1-b1bf-16320511269e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440013} {:answer/id #uuid "cb641075-be34-57f4-a864-694183e2c508" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440014}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440014} :answer-field/id #uuid "879fdc02-b39f-5138-a50a-bc9a6b50ad60" :answer-field/key "$x=-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440364} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "758